gomodel:6ab067da00010509
        a                      owl:Ontology ;
        rdfs:comment           "Model B of the two GPR179 models (curator design 2026-10-15). GPR179 ion channel regulator activity (GO:0099106) has_input TRPM1 and directly positively regulates the TRPM1 channel: Ray 2014 PMID:24790204 (Fig. 6 capsaicin-gated TRPM1 current reduced in nob5, normal in Rgs7/Rgs11 DKO, so independent of the RGS anchoring in Model A gomodel:6ab067da00008260; Fig. 3 direct interaction) and Orlandi 2013 PMID:24114537 (human GPR179 x mouse TRPM1 co-IP; PLA in retina). Mouse data -> ISS GO_REF:0000024 with MGI. Data are from rod bipolar cells; ON-bipolar cell CL:0000749 used to match Model A and the mega-viewer. Joins Model A and gomodel:6a6ba88c00000472 at TRPM1." , "Curated with GO AI HUB. GPR179 directly positively regulates TRPM1 channel gating at ON-bipolar dendritic tips." ;
        lego:conforms_to_gpad  false ;
        lego:modelstate        "development" ;
        dc:contributor         "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1522-9900" ;
        dc:date                "2026-10-23" ;
        dc:title               "GPR179 positive regulation of TRPM1 channel gating in ON-bipolar cells_Visual Perception (Human)" ;
        pav:providedBy         "http://geneontology.org" ;
        owl:versionIRI         gomodel:6ab067da00010509 ;
        biolink:in_taxon       obo:NCBITaxon_9606 .

